cially important. The supplier’s spare capacity and willingness to take extra parts at short notice are also relevant to what can be achieved.'], 'press': ['Could you help us understand how the cost estimate supports the price position when its confidence is limited and it does not cover all cost drivers?', 'Could you explain how the delivery position accounts for the recent decline in on-time performance, given the spare capacity and willingness to take extra parts at short notice?'], 'wants': ['Faster payment', 'A firm volume commitment', 'A more flexible lead-time commitment']}, 'findings': {'economics': ['At €36.39, the current price is €0.48 (1.3%) below the €36.87 should-cost estimate, so the data show no room to push below estimated cost.', 'The listed cost drivers point upward: their weighted changes contribute about 4.1 percentage points of cost pressure; their weights cover only 76% of the part.', 'The should-cost estimate has only 10% confidence, so the apparent below-cost price is uncertain.'], 'persona': ['Cash is the clearest pressure: the bank monitors monthly, the turning department is moving to short-time work, and they ask for payment within 10 days.', 'They have spare capacity and are seeking customers; sales say they can take extra parts at short notice.', 'Hollerau is an important reference customer, though repeated late payments have led them to warn they may review conditions.', 'No specific decision-maker, approval process, or frozen-price position is stated.'], 'history': ['Across three comparable negotiations, settlement was consistently 1.3 percentage points more favorable than the supplier’s ask.', 'The contract covers spacer sleeves, not the requested pump shaft, so its terms cannot be confirmed as obligations for this RFQ.', 'For the covered item, the contract sets 30-day payment, EXW delivery with a 28-day standard lead time, and annual fixed prices; price changes require 90 days’ notice.', 'There is no supplier-specific sourcing-dependency information; three suppliers are invited, but the case says there is no fallback supplier.'], 'leverage': ['On-time delivery fell from 95.8% in 2025Q4 to 88.0% in 2026Q3, supporting a push for better delivery terms.', 'The latest forecast is 2,390 units for the next 12 months, up from 450 in the March snapshot; the growing forecast may support a volume-based price request.', 'Defects improved to 318 ppm in 2026Q3 from 496 ppm in 2026Q1, and all reported quarters are class A, which supports the supplier’s case.']}}
